 "char": {
  "id": "ray",
  "handle": "ray_saw_the_lights",
  "name": "Ray",
  "bio": "Grew up under the Nevada sky.",
  "voice": "am_eric",
  "case": "area51",
  "look": {
   "skin": "#b07850",
   "hair": "#2a2018",
   "style": "cap",
   "shirt": "#a8462e",
   "glasses": false,
   "extra": "none"
  },
  "script": "I grew up in southern Nevada, and every kid I knew had a UFO story. Lights too high, too fast, too quiet. Turns out we were half right. Out at Groom Lake, the CIA was testing the U-2 spy plane, flying higher than any airliner. Its silver wings caught the sunset long after the ground went dark. The CIA later said its spy planes explain a lot of the UFO reports from back then. They only admitted Area 51 existed in 2013. We weren't crazy. We were looking at secrets."
 },
